    {
      "tag": "Sit",
      "h2": "Tables & Chairs",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>La table</strong> = the table. <strong>La chaise</strong> = the chair. Both are feminine. Sitting at your desk = 'a ma table'.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Walls",
      "h2": "Board & Door",
      "body_html": "<p><strong>Le tableau</strong> = the board. <strong>La porte</strong> = the door. <strong>La fenetre</strong> = the window. Notice <strong>le</strong> for masculine, <strong>la</strong> for feminine.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Bag",
      "h2": "Cartable",
      "body_html": "<p>A French schoolbag = <strong>un cartable</strong> (traditional satchel) or <strong>un sac a dos</strong> (backpack). Both common.</p>"
    }
  ],
